wer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117027}] :question/id #uuid "4f59c175-a7f1-58ec-b16f-fd24b9c9dd63" :question/math-academy-id "q-156685" :question/problem "Let $Π$ be the plane with equation $x - y - z = 1$ in $R^{3}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $Π$ contains the zero-vector\n2. $Π$ is closed under vector addition\n3. $Π$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n4. $Π$ is **not** a subspace of $R^{3}$"}]}
